WEBVTT

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:22.132
Iris Press Publishers The Adventures in the Grasslands by Yulia Puchkova Chapter 1 Here I am.

00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:24.602
Here I am.

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:26.443
Here I am.

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:32.586
Thinks sporty, a small, handsome baby giraffe.

00:00:32.646 --> 00:00:37.335
Mother is looking at him and listening to him.

00:00:37.395 --> 00:00:45.126
Of course, he can't talk, but she understands his every word.

00:00:45.186 --> 00:00:47.427
Who are you?

00:00:47.487 --> 00:00:49.358
Spotty asks.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:52.800
I'm your mum, she answers.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.032
My mum, he asks.

00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:58.063
Who is mum?

00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:01.065
Mum is your good friend.

00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:05.748
Mum is always with you, and you are spotty.

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:07.664
My son.

00:01:07.724 --> 00:01:10.162
Oh, great!

00:01:10.222 --> 00:01:14.246
Spotty says and smiles to Mother.

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:16.268
How are you?

00:01:16.328 --> 00:01:18.220
Mother asks.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.372
I'm hungry.

00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:22.653
Spotty answers.

00:01:22.713 --> 00:01:24.694
Don't worry.

00:01:24.754 --> 00:01:27.267
I'm not only your friend.

00:01:27.327 --> 00:01:29.849
I'm your dining room too.

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:33.122
I've got a lot of nice milk for you.

00:01:33.182 --> 00:01:37.844
Stand under me and drink, she says.

00:01:37.904 --> 00:01:42.595
Spotty, drinks and drinks.

00:01:42.654 --> 00:01:47.917
The milk is warm and tasty, and it never ends.

00:01:47.977 --> 00:01:52.708
Now he isn't hungry anymore.

00:01:52.768 --> 00:02:01.282
Mother opens her mouth, and Spotty can see a long, thick thing inside.

00:02:01.342 --> 00:02:02.943
What's that?

00:02:03.003 --> 00:02:04.504
He asks.

00:02:04.564 --> 00:02:08.347
It's my tongue, mother answers.

00:02:08.407 --> 00:02:11.641
Why is it so long?

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:15.534
Because we are giraffes.

00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:21.188
I think only giraffes have got very long tongues, Mother says.

00:02:21.248 --> 00:02:23.810
Are there many giraffes?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:28.414
Or are there only you and me, sporty asks?

00:02:28.474 --> 00:02:30.935
Mother smiles.

00:02:30.995 --> 00:02:35.388
Of course, there are a lot of giraffes.

00:02:35.448 --> 00:02:38.196
Soon we can visit them.

00:02:38.256 --> 00:02:43.466
But now I must teach you to walk and run.

00:02:43.526 --> 00:02:48.270
Spotty gets up and starts walking.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.834
What a clever baby I have got, mother laughs.

00:02:52.894 --> 00:02:55.106
Now, try to run.

00:02:55.165 --> 00:02:58.758
Spotty tries, but falls down.

00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:01.540
I've got too many legs, he says.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.786
They can't run altogether.

00:03:03.846 --> 00:03:07.933
Then tell them to run in turn, says Mother.

00:03:07.993 --> 00:03:12.717
First, your left legs run, then your right ones.

00:03:12.777 --> 00:03:16.710
Which of them are left, sporty asks.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:21.985
Can you hear a strange beat inside your body?

00:03:22.045 --> 00:03:24.547
Sporty listens.

00:03:24.607 --> 00:03:28.709
Yes, it's here.

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.769
This is your heart.

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:33.820
It's on the left.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:40.092
Your left legs are on the left too, says Mother.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:45.044
Why have I got four legs and only one heart?

00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:46.634
Sporty asks.

00:03:46.694 --> 00:03:49.885
And why is it on the left?

00:03:49.945 --> 00:03:52.236
Nobody knows.

00:03:52.296 --> 00:03:55.759
But I think you can't run with one leg.

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:58.912
And four hearts must be too noisy.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:03.245
Spotty looks in his mum's eyes.

00:04:03.304 --> 00:04:06.617
They are big and clever.

00:04:06.677 --> 00:04:09.970
And they are very kind.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.802
Let's play, son," she says.

00:04:13.862 --> 00:04:18.742
They start walking to a tall tree.

00:04:18.802 --> 00:04:24.963
Spotty can't walk fast, but Mother is walking behind him.

00:04:25.023 --> 00:04:32.468
When they come to the tree, Spotty cries, I'm the first.

00:04:32.528 --> 00:04:35.679
He is happy.

00:04:35.739 --> 00:04:51.324
Chapter 2 My family.

00:04:51.383 --> 00:04:52.754
Hi.

00:04:52.814 --> 00:04:54.544
My name is Jack.

00:04:54.604 --> 00:04:57.815
I'm a boy and I'm 12.

00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:00.936
I live with my parents in Africa.

00:05:00.996 --> 00:05:03.706
My parents are scientists.

00:05:03.766 --> 00:05:07.278
They know a lot about African animals.

00:05:07.338 --> 00:05:09.948
I have got a sister.

00:05:10.008 --> 00:05:12.228
Her name is Jill.

00:05:12.288 --> 00:05:14.710
She is 23.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.152
Jill doesn't live with us.

00:05:18.212 --> 00:05:21.954
She lives with her husband, Bill.

00:05:22.014 --> 00:05:25.156
I don't like Bill.

00:05:25.216 --> 00:05:29.998
If Jill wants something, Bill always does it.

00:05:30.058 --> 00:05:34.222
Sometimes these are very silly or bad things.

00:05:34.282 --> 00:05:39.454
One day, I'm visiting my sister and her husband.

00:05:39.514 --> 00:05:46.994
We're having coffee when suddenly she says, Bill, I want to have a pet giraffe.

00:05:47.054 --> 00:05:50.648
Bill's eyes get very big.

00:05:50.708 --> 00:05:53.000
He hasn't got a face now.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.112
Only eyes.

00:05:55.172 --> 00:05:56.803
Yes.

00:05:56.863 --> 00:06:01.047
A pet giraffe repeats my sister.

00:06:01.106 --> 00:06:02.678
It can live in the hall.

00:06:02.738 --> 00:06:05.180
Our hall is very big.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.372
Bill's eyes get normal.

00:06:07.432 --> 00:06:14.688
And he says, Okay, dear, I think I can get you a giraffe.

00:06:14.748 --> 00:06:17.529
Where do you want to get it?

00:06:17.589 --> 00:06:19.149
I ask him.

00:06:19.209 --> 00:06:22.760
In the grasslands, of course, he answers.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.160
We can't buy a giraffe.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.641
We haven't got much money.

00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:31.002
You mustn't do that, I cry.

00:06:31.062 --> 00:06:34.493
You can have serious problems with the police.

00:06:34.553 --> 00:06:35.870
Why?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:40.309
I can find a stray cat or a stray dog in the street.

00:06:40.368 --> 00:06:44.200
Why can't I find a stray giraffe?"

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.491
I look at Bill.

00:06:46.551 --> 00:06:50.843
Sometimes he is very silly.

00:06:50.902 --> 00:06:55.224
And it is all because of my sister.

00:06:55.283 --> 00:07:01.516
Jack, don't tell our parents about it, Jill asks, please.

00:07:01.576 --> 00:07:04.446
And she smiles at me.

00:07:04.506 --> 00:07:09.838
I think you can't hide a giraffe in the house, I say.

00:07:09.898 --> 00:07:15.213
I stand up, say goodbye to them, and walk to the door.

00:07:15.272 --> 00:07:20.066
But suddenly, I have an idea.

00:07:20.126 --> 00:07:25.440
Bill, can you take me with you?

00:07:25.499 --> 00:07:28.942
I can help you to catch the giraffe.

00:07:29.002 --> 00:07:31.794
Great, says Bill.

00:07:31.854 --> 00:07:37.756
Tomorrow, at six o'clock in the morning.

00:07:37.816 --> 00:07:43.596
This night I can't sleep.

00:07:43.656 --> 00:07:49.030
I am thinking about my bad sister and silly bill.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:53.642
I am thinking about that poor giraffe too.

00:07:53.702 --> 00:07:57.204
Giraffes must live in the grasslands.

00:07:57.264 --> 00:08:02.827
They are tall, big and strong, and they must walk free.

00:08:02.887 --> 00:08:06.109
They must have a lot of trees around.

00:08:06.169 --> 00:08:09.072
They love eating fresh leaves.

00:08:09.132 --> 00:08:16.469
And if people want to look at them, they can watch a film or go on a safari.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:24.044
It is very wrong to catch giraffes and put them in cages or houses.

00:08:24.104 --> 00:08:27.367
Then I'm not thinking anymore.

00:08:27.426 --> 00:08:34.932
I am sleeping.

00:08:34.992 --> 00:08:47.848
Chapter 3 Preparations My alarm clock rings.

00:08:47.908 --> 00:08:49.488
I wake up.

00:08:49.548 --> 00:08:52.370
It is sunny and hot.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.690
I am happy.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.282
It is the first day of the summer holidays.

00:08:59.342 --> 00:09:01.353
I am free.

00:09:01.414 --> 00:09:05.004
I can swim or play football.

00:09:05.065 --> 00:09:11.483
Suddenly, I remember my sister and her silly husband.

00:09:11.543 --> 00:09:15.911
They want to have a pet giraffe.

00:09:15.971 --> 00:09:20.754
Today, Bill is going to the grasslands.

00:09:20.814 --> 00:09:24.826
He wants to catch a nice baby giraffe.

00:09:24.886 --> 00:09:27.428
And I am going with him.

00:09:27.488 --> 00:09:31.790
I hope he can't catch it.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:34.461
I look at the clock.

00:09:34.521 --> 00:09:36.472
It is six o'clock.

00:09:36.532 --> 00:09:38.984
My parents are at work.

00:09:39.044 --> 00:09:44.488
I get up, put on my shorts and the t-shirt.

00:09:44.548 --> 00:09:46.879
They are bright red.

00:09:46.939 --> 00:09:53.742
I don't often wear red, but today this colour can help me.

00:09:53.802 --> 00:09:59.244
Dad says giraffes can see some bright colours.

00:09:59.304 --> 00:10:02.826
I hope they can see the red colour.

00:10:02.886 --> 00:10:09.032
I put on a red cap, open the door and go out.

00:10:09.092 --> 00:10:12.496
I run to Bill and Jill's house.

00:10:12.556 --> 00:10:16.708
When I'm at their door, Bill comes out.

00:10:16.768 --> 00:10:21.391
He's wearing a brown shirt and brown shorts.

00:10:21.451 --> 00:10:28.184
He has got a green cap on his head, and green gloves on his hands.

00:10:28.244 --> 00:10:32.947
He has got a big green bag on his back.

00:10:33.007 --> 00:10:39.577
He thinks he looks like a small tree with four green leaves.

00:10:39.637 --> 00:10:43.517
A nice tree, I say.

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:45.258
Where?

00:10:45.318 --> 00:10:47.160
Bill asks.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:50.152
Opposite me, of course, I say.

00:10:50.212 --> 00:10:51.664
Aha!

00:10:51.724 --> 00:10:57.578
I'm very clever, Bill says, and smiles.

00:10:57.638 --> 00:11:02.572
Suddenly, Bill stops smiling.

00:11:02.632 --> 00:11:06.342
He's looking at my red costume.

00:11:06.402 --> 00:11:11.204
Why are you wearing red?"

00:11:11.264 --> 00:11:12.926
he asks.

00:11:12.986 --> 00:11:16.078
You don't look like a tree.

00:11:16.138 --> 00:11:19.952
But I'm not a tree, I say.

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:22.454
I'm the red light.

00:11:22.514 --> 00:11:27.960
What do you do when you see the red light in the street?

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:31.762
I stop, Bill says.

00:11:31.822 --> 00:11:34.684
I stop too, I say.

00:11:34.744 --> 00:11:46.360
Everyone stops, men and women, boys and girls, cats and dogs, and, of course, giraffes.

00:11:46.421 --> 00:11:59.705
You are great, Bill cries and smiles at me again.

00:11:59.765 --> 00:12:12.520
Chapter 4 The Hunt Starts We walk and walk.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:19.516
No, Bill is walking and I am having fun.

00:12:19.576 --> 00:12:26.231
I look around and see a lot of funny insects and small animals.

00:12:26.291 --> 00:12:33.561
Sometimes I see snakes, but I am not afraid of them.

00:12:33.621 --> 00:12:39.940
They get angry only if you hurt them or come too close.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.012
And I only look at them.

00:12:43.072 --> 00:12:47.134
Oh, there is a beautiful one.

00:12:47.194 --> 00:12:51.848
It is sleeping and shining in the sun.

00:12:51.908 --> 00:12:57.062
It looks like silver rings one around the other.

00:12:57.122 --> 00:13:02.080
When they sleep, they are so nice.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:05.748
What's the matter?

00:13:05.808 --> 00:13:09.260
Bill isn't walking anymore.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:14.842
He's standing and looking at some big animals far away.

00:13:14.902 --> 00:13:17.144
I look at them too.

00:13:17.204 --> 00:13:19.284
They're giraffes.

00:13:19.344 --> 00:13:21.626
They're great.

00:13:21.686 --> 00:13:26.168
Some giraffes are walking and shaking their long necks.

00:13:26.228 --> 00:13:31.205
The others are standing next to trees and eating leaves.

00:13:31.265 --> 00:13:34.722
Bill starts walking again.

00:13:34.782 --> 00:13:39.764
He opens his green bag and takes out a long thick rope.

00:13:39.824 --> 00:13:43.828
The rope has got a big loop at the end.

00:13:43.888 --> 00:13:47.740
My heart stops beating.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.302
I am so sorry for those beautiful animals.

00:13:52.362 --> 00:13:55.204
I must do something.

00:13:55.264 --> 00:14:02.038
But I am only twelve, and Bill is twenty-five.

00:14:02.098 --> 00:14:07.540
Suddenly, I can see a small baby giraffe.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.170
I think it's a boy.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.312
He's very young.

00:14:12.372 --> 00:14:14.932
He can't run fast.

00:14:14.993 --> 00:14:18.624
His mother is looking at him with love.

00:14:18.684 --> 00:14:21.905
She looks very happy and proud.

00:14:21.965 --> 00:14:23.776
I understand her.

00:14:23.836 --> 00:14:26.346
She's got a great baby.

00:14:26.406 --> 00:14:32.764
Her son is tall, and his skin has got dark brown spots.

00:14:32.824 --> 00:14:37.172
They look like squares with white lines around.

00:14:37.232 --> 00:14:42.216
My dad says there are many different kinds of giraffe.

00:14:42.276 --> 00:14:46.820
Here in East Africa we have three kinds.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:50.113
This kind is my favorite.

00:14:50.174 --> 00:14:54.608
Oh, I have got a name for this nice baby.

00:14:54.668 --> 00:15:02.837
It is sporty.

00:15:02.897 --> 00:15:14.938
Chapter 5 A trick.

00:15:14.998 --> 00:15:19.941
Spotty is walking with his mum.

00:15:20.001 --> 00:15:25.244
He's one or two weeks because they're not walking with other giraffes.

00:15:25.304 --> 00:15:27.786
He's too young for that.

00:15:27.846 --> 00:15:30.338
I look at Bill.

00:15:30.398 --> 00:15:31.669
Oh no.

00:15:31.689 --> 00:15:36.952
He is looking at my spotty and smiling.

00:15:37.012 --> 00:15:39.612
He likes him too.

00:15:39.672 --> 00:15:45.352
Now he starts walking to the mum and her baby.

00:15:45.412 --> 00:15:50.134
I hope giraffes are clever animals.

00:15:50.194 --> 00:15:56.476
This small walking thing, Bill, doesn't look like a tree.

00:15:56.536 --> 00:16:00.775
Trees are tall and smell nice.

00:16:00.835 --> 00:16:04.634
But Bill isn't so silly.

00:16:04.694 --> 00:16:12.280
He stops and breaks off some small twigs with juicy green leaves.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:17.513
Oh, he's holding a lot of twigs.

00:16:17.573 --> 00:16:22.066
Now he smells nice for giraffes.

00:16:22.126 --> 00:16:27.230
He walks on and I walk behind him.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:32.466
I think and think how I can stop him.

00:16:32.526 --> 00:16:36.072
Suddenly, I have an idea.

00:16:36.132 --> 00:16:41.454
You know, I am very good at making animal sounds.

00:16:41.514 --> 00:16:47.798
I put my hands to my mouth and make a terrible lion roar.

00:16:47.858 --> 00:16:54.452
Bill jumps up, drops his twigs, and turns around fast.

00:16:54.512 --> 00:16:58.158
I look afraid too.

00:16:58.218 --> 00:17:02.334
There's a lion here, he cries.

00:17:02.394 --> 00:17:03.794
He's shaking.

00:17:03.854 --> 00:17:05.915
His face is white.

00:17:05.974 --> 00:17:08.175
He looks at a tall tree.

00:17:08.235 --> 00:17:12.426
Jack, we must climb a tree, he says.

00:17:12.486 --> 00:17:18.128
That tree hasn't got low branches, so I can't understand how we can climb it.

00:17:18.188 --> 00:17:19.948
But Bill can.

00:17:20.008 --> 00:17:23.789
He is on top of the tree in a second.

00:17:23.849 --> 00:17:25.269
Wow.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:28.998
He is very strong.

00:17:29.058 --> 00:17:34.257
Now Bill is sitting in the tree and looking around.

00:17:34.317 --> 00:17:38.248
Jack, come here, he cries.

00:17:38.308 --> 00:17:41.198
But I don't want to climb a tree.

00:17:41.258 --> 00:17:43.679
It is too hot.

00:17:43.739 --> 00:17:46.380
Are there any lions?

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.230
I ask.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:52.161
I can't see any, he cries.

00:17:52.221 --> 00:17:57.312
But Bill is too afraid to climb down.

00:17:57.372 --> 00:18:00.604
I'm looking at him.

00:18:00.664 --> 00:18:05.768
He looks like a thick branch with five green leaves.

00:18:05.828 --> 00:18:11.183
It is interesting how long he can sit in a tree.

00:18:11.243 --> 00:18:14.265
I sit down on the grass.

00:18:14.325 --> 00:18:16.586
It is very hot.

00:18:16.646 --> 00:18:18.978
But I am under a tree.

00:18:19.038 --> 00:18:21.470
It's great here.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:30.280
Now I can have a rest.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:37.868
Chapter 6.

00:18:37.928 --> 00:18:40.730
A bath.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:46.910
Spotty and his mum are going to Bill's tree.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.382
They are next to it now.

00:18:50.442 --> 00:18:55.623
The mother starts eating leaves on the tree.

00:18:55.683 --> 00:18:58.524
I can see her tongue.

00:18:58.584 --> 00:19:01.754
It is so long.

00:19:01.814 --> 00:19:06.650
It is half a metre long.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:10.824
Then I look at Bill.

00:19:10.884 --> 00:19:13.325
He's shaking.

00:19:13.385 --> 00:19:15.065
Oh no!

00:19:15.125 --> 00:19:18.346
He's afraid of Spotty's mum.

00:19:18.406 --> 00:19:21.867
Or is he afraid of her big tongue?

00:19:21.927 --> 00:19:24.958
Bill hides in the leaves.

00:19:25.018 --> 00:19:29.048
But Spotty's mum eats very fast.

00:19:29.108 --> 00:19:32.860
Soon there are no leaves on the tree.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:36.092
and Bill can't hide in them.

00:19:36.152 --> 00:19:40.926
He looks down, he wants to jump, never.

00:19:40.986 --> 00:20:00.764
I open my mouth and make a terrible  The mother's tongue is next to Bill.

00:20:00.824 --> 00:20:05.136
First, it licks his head.

00:20:05.196 --> 00:20:09.430
Then, it licks his face and ears.

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:12.952
I think Bill is very clean now.

00:20:13.012 --> 00:20:18.596
Then, Sporty's mum puts her tongue away and looks at Bill.

00:20:18.656 --> 00:20:24.090
He is wet, and he's afraid too.

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.659
Suddenly, he smiles at the mother.

00:20:27.719 --> 00:20:30.546
She looks very surprised.

00:20:30.606 --> 00:20:35.260
It is the first time a tree smiles at her.

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.192
She gets angry.

00:20:37.252 --> 00:20:38.483
Oh no!

00:20:38.543 --> 00:20:42.966
She starts shaking the tree with her horns and neck.

00:20:43.026 --> 00:20:45.608
Poor Bill.

00:20:45.668 --> 00:20:52.144
He is holding by the branches, but the mother is very strong.

00:20:52.204 --> 00:20:54.597
Now I am afraid too.

00:20:54.657 --> 00:20:59.720
If Bill falls down, he can break his neck.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:05.871
Suddenly, Spotty puts his nose to his mum.

00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:09.432
His thirsty, he wants his milk.

00:21:09.492 --> 00:21:14.583
So she stops shaking the tree and licks Spotty.

00:21:14.643 --> 00:21:20.344
Bill climbs down the tree very fast and runs to me.

00:21:20.404 --> 00:21:23.604
He hides behind my tree.

00:21:23.664 --> 00:21:28.504
He looks ugly, but happy.

00:21:28.564 --> 00:21:31.226
Oh, Jack!

00:21:31.286 --> 00:21:36.459
This mother giraffe is terrible, he cries.

00:21:36.519 --> 00:21:39.902
I think he is terrible.

00:21:39.962 --> 00:21:42.693
But I don't say it to him.

00:21:42.753 --> 00:21:45.214
I am looking at my giraffes.

00:21:45.274 --> 00:21:47.506
They are eating.

00:21:47.566 --> 00:21:51.514
The mother is four meters tall.

00:21:51.574 --> 00:21:55.272
She needs a lot of leaves to be so big.

00:21:55.332 --> 00:21:59.885
And Spotty needs a lot of milk to be like his mum.

00:21:59.946 --> 00:22:04.318
Eat, dear Spotty, eat and grow fast.

00:22:04.378 --> 00:22:07.000
Then no silly bill can catch you.

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:24.449
Chapter 7 Do you like insects?

00:22:24.509 --> 00:22:28.092
I'm watching spotty.

00:22:28.152 --> 00:22:30.553
He is so cute.

00:22:30.613 --> 00:22:33.275
He isn't drinking milk anymore.

00:22:33.335 --> 00:22:34.956
He's jumping.

00:22:35.016 --> 00:22:38.008
He wants to play.

00:22:38.068 --> 00:22:42.120
Now I can see a shadow.

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:48.663
It is the shadow of a rope with a loop.

00:22:48.723 --> 00:22:57.346
Bill is holding it and coming to the giraffes.

00:22:57.406 --> 00:23:01.228
He's hiding behind every bush.

00:23:01.288 --> 00:23:06.070
He is very slow.

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:11.724
Suddenly, Spotty's mum starts running.

00:23:11.784 --> 00:23:14.445
Spotty runs with her.

00:23:14.505 --> 00:23:19.758
Soon, they're far from Bill and me.

00:23:19.818 --> 00:23:22.990
I look at Bill.

00:23:23.050 --> 00:23:25.642
He isn't hiding anymore.

00:23:25.702 --> 00:23:27.713
He is angry.

00:23:27.773 --> 00:23:30.864
He can't catch them again.

00:23:30.924 --> 00:23:34.566
I climb a tree and look around.

00:23:34.626 --> 00:23:36.988
I can see my giraffes.

00:23:37.048 --> 00:23:39.238
They are running and playing.

00:23:39.298 --> 00:23:42.350
They look so funny now.

00:23:42.411 --> 00:23:46.472
But they are running in a circle.

00:23:46.532 --> 00:23:49.013
Soon they are coming back.

00:23:49.073 --> 00:23:51.054
They are close again.

00:23:51.114 --> 00:23:54.476
Look, Bill says.

00:23:54.536 --> 00:23:58.798
There are small birds on the mother and her baby.

00:23:58.858 --> 00:24:01.900
Do birds live on giraffes?

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.502
Of course they don't, I say.

00:24:05.562 --> 00:24:07.772
They eat on giraffes.

00:24:07.832 --> 00:24:10.524
Giraffes are their dining room.

00:24:10.584 --> 00:24:12.805
How terrible!

00:24:12.865 --> 00:24:14.246
Bill cries.

00:24:14.306 --> 00:24:18.069
I don't want to be somebody's dining room.

00:24:18.129 --> 00:24:21.332
Have you got insects in your hair?

00:24:21.352 --> 00:24:23.824
I ask.

00:24:23.884 --> 00:24:27.036
Insects in my hair?

00:24:27.096 --> 00:24:31.408
Bill looks afraid and puts his fingers in his hair.

00:24:31.468 --> 00:24:35.010
Those birds eat insects.

00:24:35.070 --> 00:24:38.481
They are their favorite food, I say.

00:24:38.542 --> 00:24:41.753
Are there insects on giraffes?

00:24:41.813 --> 00:24:43.054
Bill asks.

00:24:43.114 --> 00:24:45.356
He looks surprised.

00:24:45.416 --> 00:24:48.867
Yes, there are a lot of them.

00:24:48.928 --> 00:24:56.059
When you catch the baby and take it home, you can have a lot of insects too.

00:24:56.119 --> 00:25:04.110
So it's a good idea to take three birds with you, one for the baby and two for Jill and you.

00:25:04.170 --> 00:25:07.801
But Jill doesn't like birds, Bill says.

00:25:07.861 --> 00:25:10.951
Then I hope she likes insects, I say.

00:25:11.011 --> 00:25:13.222
No, Bill cries.

00:25:13.282 --> 00:25:15.019
She doesn't.

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:20.450
If Jill likes the giraffe, she must like its insects.

00:25:20.510 --> 00:25:24.942
There are no giraffes without insects on them.

00:25:25.002 --> 00:25:27.834
Bill starts thinking.

00:25:27.894 --> 00:25:33.898
Look, Jack, I can wash our giraffe in the bathroom.

00:25:33.958 --> 00:25:39.552
In Jill's bathroom, I laugh, are you crazy?

00:25:39.612 --> 00:25:43.606
Bill looks at me and thinks again.

00:25:43.666 --> 00:25:48.651
Then I can wash it in the garden or take it to the lake.

00:25:48.711 --> 00:25:53.951
You can have a lot of problems with that baby, I say.

00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:58.242
I'm looking at him, and he is looking at me.

00:25:58.302 --> 00:26:01.934
Poor Bill, he loves my sister.

00:26:01.994 --> 00:26:05.044
He's ready to do everything for her.

00:26:05.104 --> 00:26:07.665
Birds can't change it.

00:26:07.725 --> 00:26:17.073
Even terrible insects can't change it.

00:26:17.133 --> 00:26:29.082
Chapter 8 A strange animal.

00:26:29.142 --> 00:26:33.404
Now build is a strange thing.

00:26:33.464 --> 00:26:40.986
He ties a long branch to the back of his neck and head.

00:26:41.046 --> 00:26:46.928
Then he puts his hands on the grass.

00:26:46.988 --> 00:26:52.470
Now he has got four legs and a long neck.

00:26:52.530 --> 00:26:55.764
But there's no head on that neck.

00:26:55.824 --> 00:26:58.696
Only some twigs.

00:26:58.756 --> 00:27:03.820
I think Spotty's mum is very clever.

00:27:03.880 --> 00:27:09.334
She can't make friends with a giraffe with twigs instead of a head.

00:27:09.394 --> 00:27:12.968
But Bill can't understand that.

00:27:13.028 --> 00:27:19.723
He hasn't got a head now, and he can't think.

00:27:19.783 --> 00:27:26.389
sporty and mother are walking.

00:27:26.449 --> 00:27:31.372
Suddenly they see two big giraffes.

00:27:31.432 --> 00:27:34.756
They are very tall.

00:27:34.816 --> 00:27:41.080
They're standing together and hitting each other with their necks.

00:27:41.140 --> 00:27:44.042
What are they doing?

00:27:44.103 --> 00:27:46.354
Asks sporty.

00:27:46.414 --> 00:27:49.582
Is it a game?

00:27:49.643 --> 00:27:54.392
They're fighting, Mother says.

00:27:54.452 --> 00:27:56.806
Is it good or bad?

00:27:56.866 --> 00:27:59.118
Ask sporty.

00:27:59.178 --> 00:28:04.164
Old big giraffe sometimes fights, Mother says.

00:28:04.224 --> 00:28:06.746
Why?

00:28:06.806 --> 00:28:09.430
Stand and look.

00:28:09.490 --> 00:28:11.392
And I must eat.

00:28:11.452 --> 00:28:13.670
I'm very hungry.

00:28:13.730 --> 00:28:18.442
So mother starts eating acacia leaves.

00:28:18.502 --> 00:28:21.445
They are giraffes favorite food.

00:28:21.505 --> 00:28:25.680
And sporty is looking at the big giraffes.

00:28:25.740 --> 00:28:28.978
They fight and fight.

00:28:29.038 --> 00:28:31.653
Now they're very tired.

00:28:31.713 --> 00:28:36.206
Suddenly, one giraffe turns and walks away.

00:28:36.266 --> 00:28:38.156
He looks sad.

00:28:38.216 --> 00:28:41.528
The other giraffe looks very proud.

00:28:41.588 --> 00:28:45.841
He goes to a beautiful lady giraffe.

00:28:45.901 --> 00:28:48.332
Look at me, he says.

00:28:48.392 --> 00:28:50.294
I'm so strong.

00:28:50.354 --> 00:28:52.855
My neck is so long.

00:28:52.915 --> 00:28:56.577
My spots are so dark.

00:28:56.636 --> 00:28:58.914
I'm a cool boy.

00:28:58.974 --> 00:29:01.422
And you're a cool girl.

00:29:01.482 --> 00:29:04.414
Let's be together.

00:29:04.474 --> 00:29:08.956
But the lady giraffe doesn't look at him.

00:29:09.017 --> 00:29:11.748
She eats and eats.

00:29:11.808 --> 00:29:16.642
So the big giraffe gets very sad and goes away.

00:29:16.702 --> 00:29:18.188
Mom?

00:29:18.248 --> 00:29:22.496
That lady giraffe is silly, spotty says.

00:29:22.556 --> 00:29:26.498
When I grow up, I don't want to fight for girls.

00:29:26.558 --> 00:29:28.719
I have my lady giraffe.

00:29:28.779 --> 00:29:30.500
It's you.

00:29:30.560 --> 00:29:34.232
And he licks mother.

00:29:34.292 --> 00:29:37.284
Let's wait and see.

00:29:37.344 --> 00:29:39.726
Mother smiles.

00:29:39.786 --> 00:29:43.998
Suddenly, she stops smiling.

00:29:44.058 --> 00:29:46.842
She's looking at something.

00:29:46.902 --> 00:29:50.178
Sporty looks at it too.

00:29:50.238 --> 00:29:53.590
There is a strange animal there.

00:29:53.650 --> 00:29:55.782
What's that?

00:29:55.842 --> 00:29:58.464
Asks sporty.

00:29:58.524 --> 00:30:01.206
I don't know, mother answers.

00:30:01.266 --> 00:30:03.368
It's a very strange animal.

00:30:03.428 --> 00:30:06.079
Trees grow out of its neck.

00:30:06.140 --> 00:30:09.292
I'm afraid, cries sporty.

00:30:09.352 --> 00:30:10.984
You're right.

00:30:11.044 --> 00:30:17.241
Never come up to strange animals, even if your favourite food grows out of them.

00:30:17.301 --> 00:30:20.145
Let's run away," says Spotty.

00:30:20.205 --> 00:30:24.778
Spotty and Mother run very fast.

00:30:24.838 --> 00:30:31.862
Bill is standing on his hands and feet and looking at them.

00:30:31.922 --> 00:30:37.004
They don't like me, he says to me.

00:30:37.064 --> 00:30:47.779
I understand them, but I don't say it to Bill.

00:30:47.840 --> 00:31:01.847
Chapter 9 A Waterhole Spotty's mum is thirsty.

00:31:01.908 --> 00:31:05.850
I know that because she's going to a waterhole.

00:31:05.910 --> 00:31:08.352
The waterhole is big.

00:31:08.413 --> 00:31:11.044
But there's a lot of mud around it.

00:31:11.105 --> 00:31:13.826
It's very bad for giraffes.

00:31:13.886 --> 00:31:18.971
They can fall in the mud and often can't get up.

00:31:19.030 --> 00:31:22.321
Then they die there.

00:31:22.381 --> 00:31:26.172
I'm very afraid for Spotty and his mum.

00:31:26.231 --> 00:31:29.032
But Bill is happy.

00:31:29.092 --> 00:31:31.794
Great, he cries.

00:31:31.854 --> 00:31:36.966
When they're in the mud, we can catch the baby.

00:31:37.026 --> 00:31:43.097
Again, he ticks the rope in his hands and goes to the waterhole.

00:31:43.158 --> 00:31:46.498
I can't stop Spotty's mum.

00:31:46.558 --> 00:31:48.619
She's in the mud now.

00:31:48.679 --> 00:31:54.112
But she saves something to Spotty because he doesn't go after her.

00:31:54.172 --> 00:31:56.772
He walks around the mud.

00:31:56.832 --> 00:31:59.794
Now the mother stops.

00:31:59.854 --> 00:32:03.496
She puts her legs far from each other.

00:32:03.556 --> 00:32:07.217
Then she puts her neck down.

00:32:07.277 --> 00:32:10.568
Now her mouth can get the water.

00:32:10.628 --> 00:32:16.625
She looks very funny when she's drinking like that.

00:32:16.685 --> 00:32:25.442
It's time to catch the baby, Bill says, his mum can't help him.

00:32:25.502 --> 00:32:29.642
I don't know what to do, but I must do something.

00:32:29.702 --> 00:32:33.473
So I say, who knows?

00:32:33.533 --> 00:32:36.254
She's strong and runs fast.

00:32:36.314 --> 00:32:38.764
Let's catch her first.

00:32:38.824 --> 00:32:44.396
Bill looks at the mother, and then at a big tree next to the mud.

00:32:44.456 --> 00:32:46.266
You're right.

00:32:46.326 --> 00:32:49.454
We should tie her to that tree, he says.

00:32:49.514 --> 00:32:53.924
Bill gets the rope, and we come up to the mud.

00:32:53.984 --> 00:32:58.028
Bill wants to throw the loop around the mother's neck.

00:32:58.088 --> 00:33:02.870
But I say, the rope is too short.

00:33:02.930 --> 00:33:05.902
You must stand in the mud.

00:33:05.962 --> 00:33:10.405
Bill looks at the rope, and then at Spotty's mum.

00:33:10.466 --> 00:33:13.922
He walks into the mud.

00:33:13.982 --> 00:33:17.309
Now you stay here, I say.

00:33:17.369 --> 00:33:20.700
I must run round and stand opposite her.

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:24.312
Remember, I'm the red light."

00:33:24.373 --> 00:33:27.444
Oh, I see, Bill says.

00:33:27.504 --> 00:33:31.468
Jack, you are cool.

00:33:31.528 --> 00:33:36.834
So I run around the waterhole and stand opposite Spotty's mum.

00:33:36.894 --> 00:33:39.056
I hope she can see me.

00:33:39.116 --> 00:33:41.188
Yes, she can.

00:33:41.248 --> 00:33:44.561
She stops drinking and looks at me.

00:33:44.621 --> 00:33:46.984
She can see my red colour.

00:33:47.044 --> 00:33:49.126
She doesn't like it.

00:33:49.186 --> 00:33:52.828
She turns her neck to look at Spotty.

00:33:52.888 --> 00:34:04.880
At this moment, Belle throws the rope.

00:34:04.940 --> 00:34:17.639
Chapter 10 In the mud.

00:34:17.699 --> 00:34:20.810
Oh no!

00:34:20.870 --> 00:34:24.452
The loop is around the mother's neck.

00:34:24.512 --> 00:34:27.463
But she is very strong.

00:34:27.523 --> 00:34:29.654
She doesn't fall.

00:34:29.714 --> 00:34:34.036
She starts turning her neck left and right.

00:34:34.096 --> 00:34:37.597
Bill is holding the rope.

00:34:37.658 --> 00:34:40.428
But he can't stand anymore.

00:34:40.488 --> 00:34:42.469
He falls into the mud.

00:34:42.530 --> 00:34:46.740
The mother starts turning her body.

00:34:46.801 --> 00:34:50.601
Help me, Jack!

00:34:50.661 --> 00:34:54.152
I can't swim, Christ Bill.

00:34:54.212 --> 00:34:57.042
Don't be sad, I cry.

00:34:57.102 --> 00:34:59.213
Nobody can swim in the mud.

00:34:59.273 --> 00:35:01.103
It's normal.

00:35:01.163 --> 00:35:03.524
But Bill is sad.

00:35:03.584 --> 00:35:05.544
He's sitting in the mud.

00:35:05.604 --> 00:35:08.064
He's dirty.

00:35:08.124 --> 00:35:12.268
I'm very dirty, he cries.

00:35:12.328 --> 00:35:15.432
Don't be sad, I repeat.

00:35:15.492 --> 00:35:17.784
You can't be clean in the mud.

00:35:17.844 --> 00:35:19.596
You must be dirty.

00:35:19.656 --> 00:35:21.416
It's normal.

00:35:21.476 --> 00:35:26.861
At that moment, Spotty's mum stops turning her neck.

00:35:26.921 --> 00:35:29.883
She starts walking to Bill.

00:35:29.943 --> 00:35:32.476
Bill, I cry.

00:35:32.536 --> 00:35:34.888
The mother is going to you.

00:35:34.948 --> 00:35:38.250
I don't think she wants to make friends with you.

00:35:38.310 --> 00:35:42.068
Drop the rope and get out.

00:35:42.129 --> 00:35:46.016
Bill looks at Spotty's mum.

00:35:46.076 --> 00:35:48.326
He's afraid.

00:35:48.386 --> 00:35:53.917
He drops the rope and wants to run, but he can't.

00:35:53.977 --> 00:35:57.548
Now I am afraid for Bill.

00:35:57.608 --> 00:36:00.838
Go under the mud, I cry.

00:36:00.898 --> 00:36:02.978
Bill does so.

00:36:03.038 --> 00:36:05.819
Now the mother can't see him.

00:36:05.879 --> 00:36:08.590
She walks out of the mud.

00:36:08.650 --> 00:36:12.492
Spotty runs to her.

00:36:12.553 --> 00:36:15.976
Then go to an acacia.

00:36:16.036 --> 00:36:20.338
The mother puts her long neck in the tree.

00:36:20.398 --> 00:36:23.640
She turns her head left and right.

00:36:23.700 --> 00:36:30.542
The acacia has got a lot of thorns, but they never hurt giraffes.

00:36:30.602 --> 00:36:34.264
Now the loop is around many thorns.

00:36:34.324 --> 00:36:38.676
It gets big, and then very big.

00:36:38.736 --> 00:36:42.558
Soon, Sporty's mum takes her head out of it.

00:36:42.618 --> 00:36:44.826
She's free.

00:36:44.886 --> 00:36:48.838
Hooray, I cry.

00:36:48.898 --> 00:36:52.992
At that moment I can see Bill's head above the mud.

00:36:53.052 --> 00:36:54.043
He's looking at me.

00:36:54.103 --> 00:36:56.295
Hooray, hooray, I repeat.

00:36:56.355 --> 00:36:57.066
You're here.

00:36:57.126 --> 00:36:58.678
You're okay.

00:36:58.738 --> 00:37:01.810
I'm not okay, say Bill.

00:37:01.870 --> 00:37:04.574
I haven't got my shorts anymore.

00:37:04.634 --> 00:37:06.616
They're there.

00:37:06.676 --> 00:37:12.274
And he looks down at the mud.

00:37:12.334 --> 00:37:18.990
Oh, Mummy, you are free, Christ's spotty.

00:37:19.050 --> 00:37:21.241
He's very happy.

00:37:21.301 --> 00:37:23.252
Yes, I am.

00:37:23.312 --> 00:37:25.152
Let's run away from here.

00:37:25.212 --> 00:37:27.794
It's that strange animal again.

00:37:27.854 --> 00:37:30.644
They start running.

00:37:30.705 --> 00:37:33.816
Is it a crocodile?

00:37:33.876 --> 00:37:35.986
Asks spotted.

00:37:36.047 --> 00:37:41.266
It can be because it goes under the mud, says Mother.

00:37:41.326 --> 00:37:46.207
But crocodiles haven't got long, thin tongues.

00:37:46.267 --> 00:37:50.068
And they don't catch animals with their tongues.

00:37:50.129 --> 00:37:53.280
I know, I know, Christ's body.

00:37:53.340 --> 00:37:56.061
This is a very old crocodile.

00:37:56.121 --> 00:37:58.572
It's got no teeth.

00:37:58.632 --> 00:38:02.694
That's why it catches animals with its tongue.

00:38:02.754 --> 00:38:13.716
I think you are right, my clever boy, Smiles' mother.

00:38:13.776 --> 00:38:31.418
Chapter 11 Fishing for Shorts Bill and I are in the mud.

00:38:31.478 --> 00:38:35.070
We're looking for Bill's shorts.

00:38:35.130 --> 00:38:38.741
There are some interesting things in the mud.

00:38:38.801 --> 00:38:43.852
There's a ball, a shoe and two socks.

00:38:43.913 --> 00:38:46.890
Why are they here?

00:38:46.950 --> 00:38:52.770
I think Bill isn't the first man who gets into this mud.

00:38:52.830 --> 00:38:55.752
A nice collection, I say.

00:38:55.812 --> 00:39:00.876
You can take these socks instead of your shorts.

00:39:00.937 --> 00:39:05.870
But I don't need socks, Christ Bill.

00:39:05.930 --> 00:39:08.132
Why, I ask.

00:39:08.192 --> 00:39:12.255
Look, I think they're green when they are clean.

00:39:12.316 --> 00:39:14.787
They match your gloves.

00:39:14.847 --> 00:39:17.307
Stop it, Jack.

00:39:17.367 --> 00:39:18.988
Says Bill.

00:39:19.048 --> 00:39:21.438
He's angry now.

00:39:21.498 --> 00:39:25.579
If you like these socks, you can take them.

00:39:25.639 --> 00:39:28.780
I need my shorts.

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:32.550
Bill is very sad.

00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:36.482
But I am very happy.

00:39:36.542 --> 00:39:39.822
We're not going after the giraffes.

00:39:39.882 --> 00:39:41.442
We're staying here.

00:39:41.502 --> 00:39:44.406
We must find his shorts.

00:39:44.466 --> 00:39:47.530
I look at Spotty and his mum.

00:39:47.590 --> 00:39:49.242
They aren't very far.

00:39:49.302 --> 00:39:51.914
They're eating again.

00:39:51.974 --> 00:39:55.527
Look, Jack, Bill says.

00:39:55.587 --> 00:39:59.370
Those terrible animals are eating, eating again.

00:39:59.430 --> 00:40:01.522
And I'm hungry, like a wolf.

00:40:01.582 --> 00:40:03.203
I'm dirty too.

00:40:03.264 --> 00:40:06.627
And I haven't got my shorts.

00:40:06.687 --> 00:40:11.140
Suddenly, I can feel something in the mud.

00:40:11.200 --> 00:40:13.076
I take it out.

00:40:13.136 --> 00:40:16.072
They are Bill's shorts.

00:40:16.132 --> 00:40:19.054
Bill isn't looking at me.

00:40:19.114 --> 00:40:24.328
So I put them back in the mud and sit down on them.

00:40:24.388 --> 00:40:26.750
Can you feel anything?

00:40:26.810 --> 00:40:28.790
Asks Bill.

00:40:28.850 --> 00:40:32.434
He's on his hands and knees in the mud.

00:40:32.494 --> 00:40:34.515
No, I answer.

00:40:34.575 --> 00:40:36.546
Nothing.

00:40:36.606 --> 00:40:41.090
Why are you sitting and doing nothing?

00:40:41.150 --> 00:40:42.630
Bill is angry again.

00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:44.947
Help me.

00:40:45.007 --> 00:40:49.074
I stand on my hands and knees.

00:40:49.134 --> 00:40:51.726
Bill is next to me now.

00:40:51.786 --> 00:40:54.426
I look at my giraffes again.

00:40:54.486 --> 00:40:55.827
Ray!

00:40:55.887 --> 00:40:58.328
Now they are far away.

00:40:58.388 --> 00:41:02.140
And they are close to other giraffes with their babies.

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:06.272
They all look like Spotty and his mum.

00:41:06.332 --> 00:41:09.873
Bill can't catch Spotty now.

00:41:09.934 --> 00:41:13.888
He must be afraid of so many giraffes together.

00:41:13.948 --> 00:41:17.584
I take his shorts out of mud.

00:41:17.644 --> 00:41:19.525
Look, Bill.

00:41:19.586 --> 00:41:23.209
Are they yours, I ask?

00:41:23.269 --> 00:41:28.332
Bill is very happy.

00:41:28.393 --> 00:41:30.094
Thank you, Jack.

00:41:30.154 --> 00:41:32.846
You're a good friend, he smiles.

00:41:32.906 --> 00:41:37.099
Bill tries to put on his shorts.

00:41:37.159 --> 00:41:43.078
But they are too wet and dirty.

00:41:43.138 --> 00:41:45.743
What can I do?"

00:41:45.803 --> 00:41:47.794
he asks.

00:41:47.854 --> 00:41:53.656
I think we should go home and wash our clothes, I say.

00:41:53.716 --> 00:42:01.298
At that moment we can hear a terrible noise from the sky.

00:42:01.359 --> 00:42:04.179
We look up.

00:42:04.239 --> 00:42:07.160
The sky is very black.

00:42:07.220 --> 00:42:10.962
Then it starts raining.

00:42:11.022 --> 00:42:14.196
Yes, cries Bill.

00:42:14.256 --> 00:42:20.062
He is very happy, but I am very sad.

00:42:20.122 --> 00:42:24.548
No, I say.

00:42:24.608 --> 00:42:35.570
Bill can't hear me because the rain is too noisy.

00:42:35.630 --> 00:42:43.046
Chapter 12.

00:42:43.106 --> 00:42:47.158
Two many babies.

00:42:47.218 --> 00:42:56.340
When the rain stops, we are wet, but clean.

00:42:56.400 --> 00:42:59.782
Bill is very happy.

00:42:59.842 --> 00:43:02.185
He starts singing.

00:43:02.245 --> 00:43:05.408
Where are you giraffes?

00:43:05.468 --> 00:43:13.820
I have got green gloves on my strong big hands to catch you, my friends.

00:43:13.880 --> 00:43:18.582
You've got too many friends, I say.

00:43:18.642 --> 00:43:21.592
Look there.

00:43:21.652 --> 00:43:26.713
Bill looks and sees eight or ten giraffes.

00:43:26.773 --> 00:43:29.214
Some of them are babies.

00:43:29.274 --> 00:43:32.418
Some big giraffes are sleeping.

00:43:32.478 --> 00:43:35.943
Their heads are next to their tails.

00:43:36.003 --> 00:43:39.524
My dog sleeps like that.

00:43:39.584 --> 00:43:43.096
Look, Price Bill.

00:43:43.156 --> 00:43:46.577
All the big giraffes are sleeping.

00:43:46.637 --> 00:43:49.848
We can catch the baby.

00:43:49.908 --> 00:43:52.259
Not all, I say.

00:43:52.319 --> 00:43:55.510
The big giraffe on the left isn't sleeping.

00:43:55.570 --> 00:43:57.930
It is on guard.

00:43:57.991 --> 00:44:01.387
It can't be, Bill says.

00:44:01.447 --> 00:44:04.574
giraffes are silly animals.

00:44:04.634 --> 00:44:07.324
Okay, I say.

00:44:07.384 --> 00:44:10.426
Then try to catch Spotty.

00:44:10.486 --> 00:44:12.806
Who is Spotty?

00:44:12.866 --> 00:44:15.297
asks Bill.

00:44:15.358 --> 00:44:19.059
Our baby giraffe, I answer.

00:44:19.119 --> 00:44:22.610
Only which is Spotty.

00:44:22.670 --> 00:44:26.092
The one next to the bushes says Bill.

00:44:26.152 --> 00:44:29.153
No, the one behind that tall tree.

00:44:29.213 --> 00:44:31.684
There are five baby giraffes.

00:44:31.744 --> 00:44:34.004
Bill looks and looks.

00:44:34.064 --> 00:44:38.908
Let's catch the one between the trees and the bushes, I say.

00:44:38.968 --> 00:44:41.901
Bill takes the rope and goes to the baby.

00:44:41.961 --> 00:44:43.392
The baby conceives.

00:44:43.452 --> 00:44:47.375
It turns and runs to the guard giraffe.

00:44:47.435 --> 00:44:50.377
That's bad, says Bill.

00:44:50.438 --> 00:44:52.588
We must catch another one.

00:44:52.649 --> 00:44:59.868
He goes to the bushes, but another baby looks at Bill and runs to the guard giraffe, too.

00:44:59.928 --> 00:45:04.933
They are clever, these silly giraffes, says Bill.

00:45:04.993 --> 00:45:07.644
He's angry.

00:45:07.704 --> 00:45:12.326
Let's tie the big giraffe to a tree, I say.

00:45:12.386 --> 00:45:14.796
Then we can catch a small one.

00:45:14.856 --> 00:45:19.768
No, cries Bill, not again.

00:45:19.828 --> 00:45:22.118
He looks at me.

00:45:22.178 --> 00:45:25.640
I don't like his eyes.

00:45:25.700 --> 00:45:31.304
At that moment, he sees a third baby.

00:45:31.364 --> 00:45:35.848
It is opposite a bush with big pink flowers.

00:45:35.908 --> 00:45:39.480
A baby can't see Bill.

00:45:39.540 --> 00:45:42.862
It is smelling the flowers.

00:45:42.922 --> 00:45:49.844
Aha, prize Bill, and runs to the baby.

00:45:49.904 --> 00:45:53.446
I don't know what to do.

00:45:53.506 --> 00:46:06.073
Again, I put my hands around my mouth and roar.

00:46:06.133 --> 00:46:18.392
Chapter 13 What are they doing?

00:46:18.452 --> 00:46:22.936
It is a terrible roar.

00:46:22.996 --> 00:46:27.618
But this time, Bill turned too fast.

00:46:27.678 --> 00:46:31.880
You can see my face and hands around my mouth.

00:46:31.940 --> 00:46:33.982
What are you doing?

00:46:34.042 --> 00:46:35.988
He cries.

00:46:36.048 --> 00:46:40.716
I'm sneezing," I say, and roar again.

00:46:40.776 --> 00:46:42.647
Again sneezing.

00:46:42.707 --> 00:46:43.708
I'm sorry.

00:46:43.768 --> 00:46:46.690
I always sneeze like that.

00:46:46.750 --> 00:46:51.814
Bill's face is very strange now.

00:46:51.874 --> 00:46:57.158
He puts his hands in front of him and makes fists.

00:46:57.218 --> 00:47:02.062
At that moment we can hear a terrible noise.

00:47:02.122 --> 00:47:05.896
I look behind Bill.

00:47:05.956 --> 00:47:13.040
All the big giraffes and their babies are running at us.

00:47:13.100 --> 00:47:17.141
Look out Bill, I cry.

00:47:17.202 --> 00:47:22.464
Bill looks round and sees the giraffes and jumps up.

00:47:22.524 --> 00:47:24.745
Then he starts running.

00:47:24.805 --> 00:47:26.486
I run too.

00:47:26.546 --> 00:47:28.646
We run and run.

00:47:28.706 --> 00:47:33.288
There is that muddy water hole in front of us.

00:47:33.348 --> 00:47:35.820
Jump!

00:47:35.880 --> 00:47:39.902
Bill and I cry together.

00:47:39.962 --> 00:47:45.503
We are with our heads in the mud again.

00:47:45.563 --> 00:47:51.844
When we're out of the mud, we can't see any giraffes.

00:47:51.904 --> 00:47:56.905
There are no giraffes next to the trees or bushes.

00:47:56.965 --> 00:48:01.136
There are no giraffes on the grass.

00:48:01.196 --> 00:48:05.580
But there are other animals.

00:48:05.640 --> 00:48:11.876
These animals have got very big ears.

00:48:11.936 --> 00:48:15.847
And they are very angry.

00:48:15.907 --> 00:48:22.350
They are hitting trees, and the trees are falling onto the ground.

00:48:22.410 --> 00:48:25.951
They are elephants.

00:48:26.011 --> 00:48:28.822
What are they doing?

00:48:28.882 --> 00:48:32.204
Asks bill, he's afraid.

00:48:32.264 --> 00:48:36.658
They're breaking trees, I answer.

00:48:36.718 --> 00:48:40.322
I can see that, Bill says.

00:48:40.382 --> 00:48:44.784
Why are they doing it?

00:48:44.844 --> 00:48:49.654
I'm thinking what to say.

00:48:49.714 --> 00:48:55.855
Suddenly, I've got an idea.

00:48:55.915 --> 00:49:00.116
They're playing hide and seek with the giraffes.

00:49:00.176 --> 00:49:04.796
Look, there are no giraffes.

00:49:04.856 --> 00:49:07.760
They're hiding from the elephants.

00:49:07.821 --> 00:49:09.805
Bill is surprised.

00:49:09.865 --> 00:49:11.096
How do you know?

00:49:11.156 --> 00:49:12.626
He asks.

00:49:12.686 --> 00:49:16.449
My dad knows a lot about different animals.

00:49:16.510 --> 00:49:19.221
Elephants and giraffes are good friends.

00:49:19.281 --> 00:49:21.232
They often play together.

00:49:21.292 --> 00:49:23.754
Elephants are very clever.

00:49:23.814 --> 00:49:29.308
If they break down all the trees and bushes, giraffes can't hide behind them.

00:49:29.368 --> 00:49:32.100
Then elephants find them.

00:49:32.160 --> 00:49:34.391
And what do they do?

00:49:34.452 --> 00:49:37.863
After that, asks Bill.

00:49:37.923 --> 00:49:41.924
Then elephants hide from giraffes.

00:49:41.984 --> 00:49:48.736
Only giraffes are very tall and can see very far, and elephants are too fat.

00:49:48.796 --> 00:49:53.448
So giraffes can see elephants behind trees and bushes.

00:49:53.508 --> 00:49:56.348
Where do elephants hide then?

00:49:56.408 --> 00:49:58.279
Asks bill.

00:49:58.339 --> 00:50:05.922
They jump into a waterhole and hide in the mud, I answer.

00:50:05.982 --> 00:50:18.615
This waterhole Bill's eyes get very big, and his face changes its colour, any waterhole.

00:50:18.675 --> 00:50:22.456
Only I can't see another one here, I say.

00:50:22.516 --> 00:50:26.816
Bill looks at me, then he cries.

00:50:26.876 --> 00:50:29.797
Mummy!

00:50:29.857 --> 00:50:33.028
And runs out of the mud.

00:50:33.088 --> 00:50:35.397
I run after him.

00:50:35.457 --> 00:50:37.827
We run and run.

00:50:37.887 --> 00:50:41.500
Then Bill gets tired and falls on the ground.

00:50:41.560 --> 00:50:44.152
I sit down next to him.

00:50:44.212 --> 00:50:47.103
Chapter 14.

00:50:47.164 --> 00:50:49.706
Heroin.

00:50:49.766 --> 00:51:01.280
We're sitting on the grass.

00:51:01.341 --> 00:51:08.953
Can you see any elephant?

00:51:09.013 --> 00:51:10.794
Bill asks me.

00:51:10.854 --> 00:51:14.556
No, I can't, I say.

00:51:14.616 --> 00:51:16.537
Are there any giraffes?

00:51:16.597 --> 00:51:18.678
He asks again.

00:51:18.738 --> 00:51:21.100
I look around.

00:51:21.160 --> 00:51:24.651
Now there are some giraffes close to us.

00:51:24.711 --> 00:51:28.794
I can even see Spotty and his mum.

00:51:28.854 --> 00:51:32.226
Yes, I say.

00:51:32.286 --> 00:51:39.201
Suddenly Bill says, we're so dirty.

00:51:39.262 --> 00:51:43.006
Let's go home now.

00:51:43.067 --> 00:51:47.960
Tomorrow we can take some carrots and apples with us.

00:51:48.020 --> 00:51:50.431
A great idea, I say.

00:51:50.491 --> 00:51:53.813
We should take some cabbages and watermelons, too.

00:51:53.874 --> 00:51:57.566
They're giraffes' favourite food.

00:51:57.626 --> 00:52:02.009
Are you crazy, Bill Cries?

00:52:02.069 --> 00:52:04.661
How can we take them?

00:52:04.721 --> 00:52:08.314
They're so heavy.

00:52:08.375 --> 00:52:12.688
We can roll them, I say.

00:52:12.748 --> 00:52:14.809
Bill is looking at me.

00:52:14.869 --> 00:52:17.390
I don't like his face.

00:52:17.451 --> 00:52:22.574
I think now he understands what I'm doing here.

00:52:22.634 --> 00:52:25.545
Jack, he cries.

00:52:25.605 --> 00:52:27.336
Why are you here with me?

00:52:27.396 --> 00:52:30.138
First you roar like a lioness.

00:52:30.198 --> 00:52:38.612
Then you have that silly idea to tie the mother giraffe, and now He doesn't finish.

00:52:38.672 --> 00:52:42.024
Because we can hear a terrible roar.

00:52:42.084 --> 00:52:45.416
And this time, it is real.

00:52:45.476 --> 00:52:48.658
It's the roar of an angry lioness.

00:52:48.718 --> 00:52:50.220
We look back.

00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:54.413
We can see her.

00:52:54.473 --> 00:52:59.196
The lioness looks at us.

00:52:59.256 --> 00:53:00.957
Then at the giraffes.

00:53:01.017 --> 00:53:02.798
And again at us.

00:53:02.858 --> 00:53:06.016
She's thinking which to eat.

00:53:06.076 --> 00:53:08.922
Bill's face is white.

00:53:08.982 --> 00:53:12.262
I think mine is white too.

00:53:12.322 --> 00:53:15.034
We are too afraid.

00:53:15.094 --> 00:53:17.534
We start shaking.

00:53:17.594 --> 00:53:22.306
Suddenly, Spotty's mum runs at the lioness.

00:53:22.366 --> 00:53:26.168
Her son is running between her legs.

00:53:26.228 --> 00:53:35.986
When they come up to the angry animal, the mother puts up her front legs.

00:53:36.046 --> 00:53:41.704
The lioness is afraid.

00:53:41.764 --> 00:53:51.842
She starts jumping around the giraffes, but the mother always turns with her front legs to her and tries to kick.

00:53:51.902 --> 00:53:54.084
Hooray!

00:53:54.145 --> 00:53:56.957
The lioness is too tired now.

00:53:57.017 --> 00:53:58.948
She can't fight anymore.

00:53:59.009 --> 00:54:01.511
She turns round and runs away.

00:54:01.571 --> 00:54:07.933
Spotty is looking at his brave mother.

00:54:07.993 --> 00:54:12.372
I look at Bill.

00:54:12.432 --> 00:54:14.694
He looks strange.

00:54:14.754 --> 00:54:20.005
Suddenly he gets up and walks to the giraffes.

00:54:20.066 --> 00:54:25.428
Does he want to catch them now when they're too tired?

00:54:25.488 --> 00:54:32.430
But Bill stops and puts his head and half of his body down.

00:54:32.490 --> 00:54:35.260
Oh, I understand.

00:54:35.320 --> 00:54:42.527
He is saying, thank you to the brave mother.

00:54:42.588 --> 00:54:50.956
Mum, it's that strange animal again, says Spotty.

00:54:51.016 --> 00:54:57.790
Yes, but it's smiling at us, and it hasn't got a long tongue in its mouth.

00:54:57.850 --> 00:55:01.442
And there's no tree in his neck, says Spotty.

00:55:01.502 --> 00:55:06.645
Poor animal, can't live long without a tongue.

00:55:06.705 --> 00:55:16.253
Spotty turns to a bush, takes some leaves with his tongue, and gives them to the strange animal.

00:55:16.313 --> 00:55:19.418
You can always come here, he says.

00:55:19.478 --> 00:55:22.200
And I can give you tasty leaves.

00:55:22.260 --> 00:55:27.494
Eat them and live long.

00:55:27.554 --> 00:55:32.248
Look, Jack.

00:55:32.308 --> 00:55:35.842
Your spotty is giving me a present.

00:55:35.902 --> 00:55:39.315
Giraffes are so nice.

00:55:39.375 --> 00:55:41.947
Bill takes the leaves.

00:55:42.007 --> 00:55:43.958
He looks so funny.

00:55:44.018 --> 00:55:51.312
I like him now.

00:55:51.372 --> 00:56:02.086
Chapter 15 A happy end.

00:56:02.147 --> 00:56:07.468
Bill isn't very clever, but he is kind.

00:56:07.529 --> 00:56:11.240
He can't hunt sporty anymore.

00:56:11.300 --> 00:56:13.901
He looks at me.

00:56:13.961 --> 00:56:17.062
Jack, you're right.

00:56:17.122 --> 00:56:20.163
It's wrong to catch giraffes.

00:56:20.223 --> 00:56:22.814
They must walk free.

00:56:22.874 --> 00:56:25.696
But what should I tell Jill?

00:56:25.756 --> 00:56:29.880
She can get very angry, and I love her.

00:56:29.940 --> 00:56:32.492
He sits down on the grass.

00:56:32.552 --> 00:56:34.712
He's very sad.

00:56:34.772 --> 00:56:37.814
I know what we should do, I say.

00:56:37.874 --> 00:56:40.476
Then I talk and talk.

00:56:40.536 --> 00:56:43.438
Soon Bill knows my idea.

00:56:43.498 --> 00:56:45.338
He likes it.

00:56:45.399 --> 00:56:48.642
I hope it helps, he says.

00:56:48.702 --> 00:56:52.135
So we take the rope and go home.

00:56:52.195 --> 00:56:56.526
The mud on us is dry now, and our skin hurts.

00:56:56.586 --> 00:56:59.377
So we can't walk fast.

00:56:59.437 --> 00:57:05.029
When we're in front of the door, Jill opens it and jumps up.

00:57:05.089 --> 00:57:08.540
What's the matter with you, she cries.

00:57:08.600 --> 00:57:15.882
And then we say, dear Jill, there are lots of giraffes in the grasslands.

00:57:15.942 --> 00:57:19.162
They're all very tall and beautiful.

00:57:19.222 --> 00:57:22.192
We can't choose only one.

00:57:22.252 --> 00:57:27.806
If you want a pet giraffe, let's go to the grasslands together.

00:57:27.866 --> 00:57:31.230
Then you can show us your favorite one.

00:57:31.290 --> 00:57:34.332
Only don't put on many clothes.

00:57:34.392 --> 00:57:37.034
Put on a swimming costume.

00:57:37.094 --> 00:57:40.156
Chill doesn't understand.

00:57:40.216 --> 00:57:43.398
A swimming costume.

00:57:43.458 --> 00:57:48.160
Why do I need a swimming costume there?

00:57:48.220 --> 00:57:52.850
Because there are angry lionesses there, I say.

00:57:52.910 --> 00:57:55.600
When they're hungry, they run at you.

00:57:55.660 --> 00:57:57.861
They run very fast.

00:57:57.921 --> 00:58:03.772
You can't run away from them, so you must hide in a muddy waterhole.

00:58:03.832 --> 00:58:08.754
And when you get out of the mud, your clothes are dirty.

00:58:08.814 --> 00:58:11.644
And very heavy, says Bill.

00:58:11.704 --> 00:58:13.164
Yes, I say.

00:58:13.225 --> 00:58:16.150
Then you can't walk fast in them.

00:58:16.210 --> 00:58:21.746
And when angry elephants come and start breaking trees, oh!

00:58:21.806 --> 00:58:23.637
Chills stops me.

00:58:23.697 --> 00:58:26.058
She looks afraid now.

00:58:26.118 --> 00:58:29.949
I think I don't need a pet giraffe.

00:58:30.009 --> 00:58:37.081
I've got no free time, and our house isn't very tall.

00:58:37.141 --> 00:58:40.971
We can make a big hole in the roof, I say.

00:58:41.031 --> 00:58:42.932
Are you crazy?

00:58:42.992 --> 00:58:44.312
Jill asks.

00:58:44.372 --> 00:58:47.194
I don't want any holes in my roof.

00:58:47.254 --> 00:58:48.916
I don't need a giraffe.

00:58:48.976 --> 00:58:50.558
That's all.

00:58:50.618 --> 00:58:53.700
Okay, we see.

00:58:53.760 --> 00:58:56.132
Can we go to the bathroom now?

